     * disclosure, closed the login page, or signed in to a page that set none), or `capture` ran
     * without them, before `login` or after an earlier capture used them. Call `login` again.
     */
    case NotLoggedIn
    /**
     * The capture ended before the institution's reply was frozen (the network dropped or the app
     * was suspended). That session is over: call `capture` again with the same cookies, which the SDK
     * keeps for this retry. `prove` and `claim` also return it when called out of order, such as a
     * second `prove` of one witness.
     */
    case SessionLost
    /**
     * The session was cancelled: `cancel` was called, or a verb's caller gave up on it (its Task or
     * coroutine was cancelled). `run_tree` also ends with it when the user closes its page or declines
     * its sign-in notice; the session itself is not cancelled then.
     */
    case Cancelled
    /**
     * An enclave's receipt did not match its opening. Start a new session; report it if it repeats.
     */
    case WrongEvidence
    /**
     * The institution's reply ended before its declared length.
     */
    case Truncated
    /**
     * The institution sent more than the profile allows.
     */
    case ExtraResponse
    /**
     * The institution's TLS records arrived out of order.
     */
    case Reordered
    /**
     * A size or count limit of the profile or the protocol was exceeded.
     */
    case LimitExceeded
    /**
